## Bug Description

OAI CN5G AMF v2.2.2 builds an NGAP Error Indication after receiving an `UplinkNASTransport` with a valid RAN UE NGAP ID and a mismatched AMF UE NGAP ID. The `ERROR_INDICATION` message-type case is unimplemented, and the default `MessageType` object leaves its message-type field uninitialized. In the reproduced run, encoding logged `Ngap_NGAP_PDU_PR_NOTHING (messageType encode error)`. Error Indication initialization then dereferenced a null `initiatingMessage`, terminating AMF with SIGSEGV. A peer able to reach N2/SCTP can trigger denial of service.

## To Reproduce

1. Start AMF, establish an SCTP association, and complete NG Setup.
2. Send an Initial UE Message carrying `7e005f18`.
3. Send an Uplink NAS Transport with the same RAN UE ID, mismatched AMF UE ID `0`, and NAS `7e025e710000`.

## Expected Behavior

The AMF should encode a valid Error Indication or safely handle an encoding failure while keeping the process and N2 service available.

## Observed Behavior

The AMF log records the UE ID mismatch and `Ngap_NGAP_PDU_PR_NOTHING (messageType encode error)`. The host kernel then records a segfault in `oai_amf` at address `0x20`. Docker reports `exited`, exit code `139`, and `OOMKilled=false`. The reproduction PCAP contains 14 packets; tcpdump reports zero drops.

## Root Cause

The `ERROR_INDICATION` case in `src/common-src/ngap/ngap_msgs/NgapMessage.cpp:310-312` contains only a TODO. The default `MessageType::MessageType()` constructor (`src/common-src/ngap/ngap_ies/MessageType.cpp:21-23`) initializes only criticality and leaves `m_TypeOfMessage` unset. In the observed run it evaluates to `Ngap_NGAP_PDU_PR_NOTHING`, so encoding does not allocate `initiatingMessage`. The `ErrorIndication` constructor (`ErrorIndication.cpp:19-20`) nevertheless calls `initialize()` unconditionally; `ErrorIndication.cpp:27-29` dereferences `ngapPdu->choice.initiatingMessage`.

## Environment

- OAI CN5G AMF v2.2.2
- Docker container `oai-amf`
- OS: Ubuntu 22.04.5 LTS
- Kernel version: 6.8.0-71-generic

