## Relationship to existing issue #20

Both reports have the same high-level trigger: a mismatched UE ID enters the N2 Error Indication response path. They also concern the same tested image and source revision. Issue #20 reports a later failure: after Error Indication construction, an empty TMSI reaches `FiveGSTmsi::encode()` and `std::stol("")` throws. This reproduction crashes after `messageType encode error`, before FiveGSTmsi encoding, at the null `initiatingMessage` dereference.
